#=GF RN   [3]
#=GF RM   21906956
#=GF RT   The structure of a tetrahydrofolate-sensing riboswitch reveals two ligand
#=GF RT   binding sites in a single aptamer.
#=GF RA   Trausch JJ, Ceres P, Reyes FE, Batey RT
#=GF RL   Structure. 2011;19:1413-1423.
#=GF RN   [4]
#=GF RM   24388757
#=GF RT   A disconnect between high-affinity binding and efficient regulation by
#=GF RT   antifolates and purines in the tetrahydrofolate riboswitch.
#=GF RA   Trausch JJ, Batey RT
#=GF RL   Chem Biol. 2014;21:205-216.
#=GF CC   Tetrahydrofolate (THF) riboswitch was first reported for Ames et al. [1]
#=GF CC   as an RNA motif in 5' untranslated (5'-UTR)regions of folate transport and
#=GF CC   biosynthesis genes in Firmicutes genomes. The structure of THF riboswitch
#=GF CC   has been reported in [2,3,4], it presents an inverted three-way junctional
#=GF CC   architecture. THF riboswitch presents a pseudoknot that joins P1-P2 and
#=GF CC   the loop of P3 and two THF binding. Tetrahydrofolate riboswitch structure
#=GF CC   is reported in PDB: 4LVV, 4LVW, 4LVX, 4LVY, 4LVZ, 4LW0 [4], 3SD3 [3],
#=GF CC   3SUH, 3SUX, 3SUY [2], 6Q57 and 7KD1.
#=GF WK   Tetrahydrofolate_riboswitch
#=GF SQ   101

